{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_end","contentIndex":1,"content":"Delete `-wal` and `-shm` alongside the overwrite (or truncate the WAL after checkpointing with all connections closed) — the restored file MUST NOT sit beside the old WAL.\n\nSkipping it makes SQLite replay the stale WAL into the restored database on next open: old pages reappear, and with a mismatched `-shm`/changed file size you get `SQLITE_CORRUPT`/`disk I/O error` — i.e. the restore silently reverts to pre-restore data rather than the backup.\n\nSo: stop all connections → copy sqlite → delete `brain.sqlite-wal` and `brain.sqlite-shm` → reopen and verify."}}
